```css
.parent {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  min-height: 100vh; /* parent needs a height */
}
```

Flexbox equivalent: `display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center;`

⚠ Centering fails silently if the parent has no height, so set one (like `min-height: 100vh`).

Use flexbox on the parent:

```css
.parent {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: 100vh; /* parent needs a height */
}
```

Or the shorter grid version: `display: grid; place-items: center; min-height: 100vh;`

⚠ Centering vertically does nothing if the parent has no explicit height, which is the most common reason it "doesn't work."

Use flexbox on the parent (or grid, which is shorter):

```css
.parent {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  min-height: 100vh; /* parent needs a height */
}
```

