```css
.parent {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: 100vh;
}
```

⚠ Centering fails silently if the parent has no height, so set `height` or `min-height` on it.

Use flexbox on the parent:

```css
.parent {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: 100vh;
}
```

The parent needs a defined height (here `min-height: 100vh`), or vertical centering has no space to work in.
